Tier: C (steering/narrative-adjacent, not a substitute for raw instrument
  data). See M1_DATA_ACCESS_STRATEGY.md for the raw ILL-DATA access
  pathway that would promote this dataset toward Tier B.

Known limitation (see M1_REPORT.md for full writeup): the roton-branch
parameters (Delta, Q_m) fit well against this digitization (Delta within
1.9% of Godfrin et al. 2021's literature value; Q_m within 0.3%), but the
phonon-branch slope (sound velocity c) does NOT reproduce the literature
value from this digitization (~27% low, robust across several q_max
choices) -- the near-origin curve height is small on the figure's scale,
making the true asymptotic tangent slope hard to read accurately by eye.
Recovering c reliably from this figure would need finer-grained sampling
at Q < 0.1 Angstrom^-1 than this pass attempted, or (preferably) the raw
instrument data.
